#
# kiwi-cake-runtime.service: a USER unit (systemctl --user) for the demo_runtime daemon ON THE ROBOT, run from ONE pinned
# release that bin/runtime-release.sh stage built from a `git archive` of one commit. Rendered by
# bin/runtime-release.sh render with every path absolute; no sudo, nothing system-wide. It is SEPARATE from
# bin/pi/lekiwi-deploy.sh and its APP_FILES: that script deploys the Cake resident, the host and the capability; this
# unit runs the robot-side service that carries a mission beneath them (section 3.5 of the route-(ii) design).
#
# NEVER ENABLED. This file has NO [Install] section: with no WantedBy= there is no target to enable it into, so linger can
# never start it at boot. Starting it is an operator's step, with the robot attended.
#
# SHIPPED OFF, TWICE:
#   - the runtime starts WITHOUT --enable-hardware-commands unless the operator rendered it with that flag named
#     (KC_RUNTIME_HARDWARE_COMMANDS=1), so every motion command and every mission run is refused by default;
#   - the configuration it reads ships with mission.execution UNSET, and unset answers mission_unavailable for every
#     mission op, exactly as a runtime before the robot-side execution did (demo_runtime.mission_service). Setting it is
#     the operator's decision after the attended checks, and nothing here writes the configuration.
#
# THE STOP. ExecStop first asks the runtime for its guarded stop over its own socket (the CLI's `stop`: the mission's
# cancel event, then SIGINT to the controller's pid, never more), and only then does systemd send the daemon SIGTERM.
# KillMode=process is deliberate and is the one difference from the Cake units: the controller is the runtime's child in
# its own session and its ONLY stop is that SIGINT. systemd must not SIGTERM or SIGKILL it with the daemon; a controller
# still finishing its guarded stop when the daemon ends is found again by the next daemon by its scan id and adopted, or
# finished (demo_runtime.supervisor, RECOVERY). Restart=no: a daemon that died is started again by a person, and motion
# permission, which lives only in the daemon's memory, is then confirmed again anyway.
#
# THE ENVIRONMENT. The daemon imports demo_runtime and demo_contracts from the release it was rendered for, never from a
# checkout, and each controller run is pinned again by the runtime's own bundle. PYTHONPATH names exactly those two.
[Unit]
Description=kiwi-cake-runtime: the robot-side demo runtime daemon, from one pinned release (user unit)

[Service]
Type=simple
WorkingDirectory=@@RELEASE_DIR@@
Environment=PYTHONPATH=@@RELEASE_DIR@@/packages/demo-runtime:@@RELEASE_DIR@@/packages/demo-contracts/python
Environment=PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
ExecStart=@@PYTHON@@ -m demo_runtime.daemon --config @@CONFIG@@ --data-dir @@DATA_DIR@@@@HARDWARE_FLAG@@
ExecStop=-@@PYTHON@@ -m demo_runtime.cli --data-dir @@DATA_DIR@@ stop
Restart=no
KillMode=process
KillSignal=SIGTERM
TimeoutStopSec=30
